<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Simpson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1787–1860</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Simpson was a Scottish-born governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> from 1821 until his death. After the merger with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> he reorganised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> across Rupert's Land with ruthless efficiency. He travelled widely by canoe and made an overland journey around the world in 1841–1842.</p></div>
